PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_20A03_Ash_Prompt_Vault_12ash_vault_db_10AshVaultDB_26reindex_vault, "v1.1.0 (D1): renumber prompts / prompt_images /\n        wildcard_prompts ids to 1..N (ascending order), update every\n        cross-reference, reset the AUTOINCREMENT sequences, and\n        recompute child_count - closing the ID gaps left by deletes.\n        v1.1.2: explicit BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction + SQLite >= 3.25\n        pre-check. v1.1.3 ROOT CAUSE FIX: the reference-updating step\n        re-pointed FK columns DIRECTLY old->new, which transiently\n        violates the prompt_tags COMPOSITE PRIMARY KEY (a later-\n        processed row maps onto an id still occupied by a not-yet-\n        processed row). Reference columns now use the SAME two-phase\n        +OFFSET shift as the main tables (Phase 3a up into the empty\n        1e9+ range, Phase 3b down to 1..N) - collision-free by\n        construction - plus an orphan pre-cleanup (Phase 0).\n        NOTE (v1.2.0): reindex closes ID GAPS only. It does NOT\n        remove childless \"ghost\" wildcards - they are real rows with\n        nothing to display; use repair_wildcard_links(purge_emptied)\n        for those.\n        Rule 34 WARNING: EXPLICIT operation only - saved workflows\n        that store old vault IDs (record_id widgets) will point at\n        DIFFERENT records afterwards. Never run automatically.");
