PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_20A03_Ash_Prompt_Vault_12ash_vault_db_10AshVaultDB_28repair_wildcard_links, "v1.1.4 (Issue B): one-time maintenance repair for legacy\n        wildcard child links. The pre-v1.0.2 recorder linked prompts to\n        wildcard parents with a permissive matcher (any prompt containing\n        JSON braces qualified INSTANTLY; raw-text similarity at threshold\n        0.3 let unrelated long prompts pass) - so unrelated prompts\n        (e.g. a solo JSON prompt clubbed under an unrelated wildcard\n        template) appear as \"sister images\". The v1.0.2 recorder no\n        longer CREATES such links; this method RE-VALIDATES every\n        existing prompt->wildcard link with the caller-supplied matcher\n        and NULLs the failures (the same SET-NULL semantics the FK uses\n        elsewhere). Orphaned links (prompt pointing at a deleted\n        wildcard) are cleaned as well.\n        v1.2.0 (GHOST WILDCARDS): purge_emptied=True additionally\n        DELETES every wildcard left with ZERO children. A childless\n        wildcard still counts in stats but has NOTHING to display\n        (get_wildcard_view returns no_images), so both panels render\n        it as \"Record not found\" - it looks exactly like a deleted-id\n        gap, and REINDEX CANNOT REMOVE IT (reindex closes id gaps;\n        ghosts are real rows). child_count is re-derived from the base\n        table (single source of truth) immediately before the delete.\n        The matcher is INJECTED (Rule 19/24): the DB layer stays free\n        of node-module imports (ash_prompt_vault imports VAULT_DB from\n        here - a top-level reverse import would be circular).\n        Signature: matcher(prompt, template) -> bool. dry_run=True\n        reports what WOULD change without applying. Summary reports\n        wildcards_emptied (became empty via unlink) and purged (deleted\n        ghosts, when purge_emptied). Returns (ok, summary).");
